==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|hanef}}, {{m|gmh|hanif}}, {{m|gmh|hanf}}, from {{inh|de|goh|hanaf}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*hanapi}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*hanapiz}}. Compare {{cog|nl|hennep}}, {{cog|en|hemp}}, {{cog|da|hamp}}. Also cognate with {{cog|grc|κάνναβις}}, whence the doublet {{m|de|Cannabis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/hanf/}} (standard)
* {{IPA|de|/hamf/}} (colloquial, regional)
* {{audio|de|De-Hanf.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|g2=n|Hanfes|gen2=Hanfs|-}}

# [[hemp]]
# hemp as a [[drug]] or medical substance
#: {{syn|de|Cannabis|Marihuana}}

====Usage notes====
* The neuter gender is rare, but is sometimes found when referring to the use as a drug (after the two synonyms above, which are both neuter).

